 "markdown": "## Summary\nI'll add a \"Close\" button to the left of \"Next\" in the page header. Clicking it navigates to the application home page (the dashboard).\n\n## How it works today\nThe page header is rendered by `oj-sp-general-overview-page`, which shows a single primary action \"Next\" via `primary-action` wired to `$listeners.nextToCatalog` → `NavigateToCatalogChain`. There is no secondary/close button today. The JSON `imports` already includes `oj-button`.\n\n## What changes\n`oj-sp-general-overview-page` exposes a `toolbar` slot for extra header actions. I'll place a \"Close\" `oj-button` in that slot, wired to a new `closeRequest` event listener → a new `GoHomeChain` that navigates to the application's default/home page using the `vb/action/actions` `navigateToPage` action with the special `__default` page target (the app's home). Navigation must happen in a chain, not inline in a binding.\n\n## The change\n- `webApps/vbredwoodapp/flows/customer-portal/pages/project-create-request-page.html` — add a \"Close\" `oj-button` in the header `toolbar` slot, wired to `$listeners.closeRequest`.\n- `webApps/vbredwoodapp/flows/customer-portal/pages/project-create-request-page.json` — declare the `closeRequest` event listener pointing at `GoHomeChain`.\n- `webApps/vbredwoodapp/flows/customer-portal/pages/project-create-request-page-chains/GoHomeChain.js` — new chain that navigates to the application home page.\n\n## After the change\nOn the Create Equipment Request page, the user sees a \"Close\" button immediately to the left of \"Next\" in the header. Clicking \"Close\" leaves the form and takes them to the application's home page.\n\n## Risks\n- The exact \"home\" target depends on the app's default page configuration. I use `navigateToPage` with `page: '__default'`, which VBCS resolves to the application's configured default (home) page. If the app's home is a specific named flow/page rather than the default, this target may need adjusting — see Questions.\n- No other pages use `GoHomeChain` (it's new), so no cross-page impact.\n\n## How to test\n1. Open the Create Equipment Request page.\n2. Confirm a \"Close\" button appears immediately to the left of \"Next\" in the header.\n3. Click \"Close\".\n4. Confirm the app navigates to the home page and the form is left.\n\n## Questions\nNone — proceeding with the application default (home) page as the target. If your home is a specific named page, tell me its flow/page name and I'll point `GoHomeChain` at it.",
